From ff47ce925972cbba2647180b0c094e7139a7a1ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:11:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Exclude BitTorrent setting (#72)

Add "Exclude BitTorrent" setting (#72)

Adds settings.exclude_bittorrent (default off). When enabled, sniffed
BitTorrent/DHT traffic is routed to bypass-out right after sniffing and
before any section rule, so torrent clients keep working without being
proxied. HTTP/HTTPS trackers still follow section rules.

Ported from Gavr1024/forkop-mod, where the same sing-box rule is used.
The option is part of the sing-box runtime signature, so toggling it
regenerates the config. Checked with sing-box 1.12.25, 1.13.21 and
1.14.2 (`sing-box check`).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HEQfjBzS7Wos7AvTk18TDQ
